#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096502 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96967f25-565a-5338-878e-00fd30055772" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Below a Curve and Above the X-Axis"}] :question/id #uuid "dc29cf6e-4f68-552e-ae7a-f9834eec1bd7" :question/math-academy-id "e-781" :question/problem "Find the area between the curve $y=x^2-2x+2,$ the $x$-axis, and the lines $x=0$ and $x=2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/assets/6b85f10cde49017eac1c56ad1b8abbcdf3033a367d5e1eb162dd89fbb6141461.png)" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}({x}^{2}-2x+2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-2{\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x+2{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{0}^{2}-2\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}|}_{0}^{2}+2x{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{8}{3}-0)-2(2-0)+2(2-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}-4+4 \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096503 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ad216da-1bcf-5b87-9436-918ef1e5015a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Above a Curve and Below the X-Axis"}] :question/id #uuid "5893a692-573a-5e1a-81aa-db34fa6059ed" :question/math-academy-id "e-782" :question/problem "Find the area of the closed region between the curve $y=x^2-1$ and the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the intersections of the curve with the $x$-axis:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-1 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2} & =1 \\\\ x & =\\pm 1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe draw a sketch of the region, as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/assets/9b78aad41f84f6a6997914bd8d4243f30cb0ebea4edb5305962dc11c7a46a807.png)\n\nWe want the area between the curve $y=x^2-1$ and the $x$-axis, from $x=-1$ to $x=1.$ To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}({x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{-1}^{1}-x{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{3}-(-\\frac{1}{3}))-(1-(-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}-2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $\\dfrac{4}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286979 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ad216da-1bcf-5b87-9436-918ef1e5015a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Above a Curve and Below the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02d2d42c-a2f6-5794-98d1-e9f45e363f20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286981} {:answer/id #uuid "8aaa62df-b3d3-5788-932b-ac74df33f711" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286982} {:answer/id #uuid "6c04dcf5-bb0e-519d-bea6-29b3eaafd011" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286983} {:answer/id #uuid "8a2f18ac-79ee-5da0-af4b-3b111f5d3115" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286984} {:answer/id #uuid "edb5b488-bf49-5b1d-877c-a110c0b28fc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286985}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8aaa62df-b3d3-5788-932b-ac74df33f711" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286982} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d637e68-da4f-5b6c-a95a-d87f9ad2692b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286980}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0c21d4e0-baa2-59e6-b265-1bfdd4a8ba84" :question/math-academy-id "q-103824" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/assets/97cf633bce7a8eeef443757e62d52f356c911b6aee3d8019d434d514416b0049.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x$ and the $x$-axis between $x=-\\pi $ and $x=0$, as shown above. What is the area of the region?" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\pi }^{0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{|}_{-\\pi }^{0} \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)-(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-\\pi )) \\\\  & =-1-(1) \\\\  & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304549 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96967f25-565a-5338-878e-00fd30055772" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Below a Curve and Above the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a1ed6507-0667-5fe4-8a0b-5a321a99264b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{20}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304551} {:answer/id #uuid "41c6f5cf-683c-5ae9-8702-81d2222ae093" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{27}{64}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304552} {:answer/id #uuid "853e5b7c-ad0d-51f9-a854-2c5ea1c52749" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{83}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304553} {:answer/id #uuid "b3cabd0a-bcd0-5285-9d5d-8e9d38961259" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{41}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304554} {:answer/id #uuid "2d67f8a0-3e1b-5e88-b60d-8f4ed692641e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{91}{20}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304555}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b3cabd0a-bcd0-5285-9d5d-8e9d38961259" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{41}{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304554} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ee952cf-3b38-5102-bb1f-b7500cc2ed7a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304550}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4167f5cf-9f6d-51bc-8664-d6f3f133f408" :question/math-academy-id "q-11020" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/assets/36a6f536866d34703f0900304a5859518461fdf0d8c1df42e5269a253c9c3ff2.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y=-2{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}-2$, the $x$-axis and the lines $x=1$ and $x=2$, shown above." :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(-2{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}-2)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+7{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-2{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}|}_{1}^{2}+7\\cdot {\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{1}^{2}-2\\cdot x{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =-2(\\frac{(2)^{4}}{4}-\\frac{1}{4})+7(\\frac{(2)^{3}}{3}-\\frac{1}{3})-2(2-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{15}{2}+\\frac{49}{3}-2 \\\\  & =\\frac{41}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186286993 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96967f25-565a-5338-878e-00fd30055772" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Below a Curve and Above the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7ad04aee-4354-5499-a9c4-5d32782153cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{3}+\\ln(2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286995}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7ad04aee-4354-5499-a9c4-5d32782153cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{3}+\\ln(2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286995} :answer-field/id #uuid "cfbc56d0-6cf5-56e8-832a-e1f5ce426489" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286994}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3dc8a6c1-7592-5eeb-a313-53d3c7edaf54" :question/math-academy-id "q-316022" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/assets/b5432ed129d85a3718f8e5ebe0cca141731c366d1b32e8e72d0916c60c34de2c.png)\n\nA region in the $x$-$y$ plane is bounded by the curve $y={sec}^{2}⁡x+\\frac{1}{x}$, and the $x$-axis between $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$, as shown above. \nFind the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}({sec}^{2}⁡(x)+\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{sec}^{2}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(x)+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)){|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =(\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{3}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{3})-(\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{3}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\frac{\\pi /3}{\\pi /6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{3}}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304556 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96967f25-565a-5338-878e-00fd30055772" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Below a Curve and Above the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2465abe2-d60c-50de-ba70-347ec4490ee4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304558} {:answer/id #uuid "b9fba83f-4290-5b40-b396-bfcc44aeff34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304559}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b9fba83f-4290-5b40-b396-bfcc44aeff34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304559} :answer-field/id #uuid "df52829b-59f8-5d84-90ef-64a9787ae8a4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304557}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ee59a109-b2bd-5098-8f6c-967dab2c90fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-345321" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/assets/2102626f331aaa7803462f8e427ef2c0150deb554955199f3d402123934e815a.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y={x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+3$ and the $x$-axis between $x=-1$ and $x=1$, as shown above. Find the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}({x}^{3}-2{x}^{2}+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}-2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+3x){|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{2}{3}+3)-(\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{2}{3}-3) \\\\  & =\\frac{31}{12}-(-\\frac{25}{12}) \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287002 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96967f25-565a-5338-878e-00fd30055772" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Below a Curve and Above the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2234af5-c4b4-528e-a73d-9112c3bcf211" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287004} {:answer/id #uuid "dd04ae4e-8b2a-583a-99ac-cefd48c3c441" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287005}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd04ae4e-8b2a-583a-99ac-cefd48c3c441" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287005} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a308356-6fe7-5b58-823a-c078c0fdfb17" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287003}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7dc244c3-54c6-5170-b8f9-917b4e9e083b" :question/math-academy-id "q-345322" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/assets/66bf8c1144de1ad65938345d2937fddd6fb43ec4822a2b98a9b5383ca2609567.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=-2{x}^{2}+3$ and the $x$-axis between $x=0$ and $x=1$, as shown above. Find the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-2{x}^{2}+3)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(-2\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}+3x){|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(-\\frac{2}{3}+3)-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287006 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ad216da-1bcf-5b87-9436-918ef1e5015a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Above a Curve and Below the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e1f9a6a-e10b-58a2-a01b-182ae2eeed8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287008} {:answer/id #uuid "25f991f6-3353-56a2-83b3-1b27ebe7a8a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304560}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0e1f9a6a-e10b-58a2-a01b-182ae2eeed8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{8}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287008} :answer-field/id #uuid "8715be83-ce41-55ca-9341-52a474fd23f8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287007}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "10fa10cd-fc6f-507a-99f5-6fa17f1da5d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-345343" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/assets/34eb73b6bd93f9a45b666ed0599719a09b54948d1d81b14ceea9b46f99b75054.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y=-{x}^{2}-1$, the $x$-axis, and the line $x=-1$ and $x=1$ (shown above). Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}(-{x}^{2}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{-1}^{1}\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{-1}^{1}-x{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =-(\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{(-1)^{3}}{3})-(1-(-1)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{2}{3}-2 \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is \n\n$$\nA=-{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{8}{3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304561 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ad216da-1bcf-5b87-9436-918ef1e5015a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Above a Curve and Below the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4cc25586-ebac-5b08-92c1-0da3e689842a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304563} {:answer/id #uuid "797e665b-c83f-5bae-bfb9-18eaa7f1cfea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304564}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "797e665b-c83f-5bae-bfb9-18eaa7f1cfea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304564} :answer-field/id #uuid "96ab2319-8b24-5616-a0b6-4e7b27e531ba" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304562}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1ce635ef-dd49-5b27-ab90-ab2605396353" :question/math-academy-id "q-406820" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/assets/31db08aa86f46d6601820b34dd938bc4b3738cba90f2fdd2721b4eb2069fa40b.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$, the $x$-axis and the lines $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$, as shown above. Find the area $A$ of the region. Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2}(-\\operatorname{csc}⁡x\\operatorname{cot}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡x{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{2}-\\operatorname{csc}⁡\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =1-2 \\\\  & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is \n\n$$\nA=-{\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x=1.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304565 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "96967f25-565a-5338-878e-00fd30055772" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Below a Curve and Above the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b1700c8-ebb4-5dbb-b5cb-e125921de9e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{sin}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304567} {:answer/id #uuid "a5606232-472f-524c-bdd6-6bbc6c44b70e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{sin}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304568} {:answer/id #uuid "31a1f447-87ee-547b-b868-fcfd68bf25d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{cos}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304569} {:answer/id #uuid "c290a8b2-23f9-5759-b431-05840a83c0eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304570} {:answer/id #uuid "082e07de-fbd0-5926-a9a8-cc87e8d22068" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡2\\pi +\\operatorname{cos}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304571}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "31a1f447-87ee-547b-b868-fcfd68bf25d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{cos}⁡1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304569} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d114066-46c2-5f55-aff3-ee0e9c8d2261" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304566}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ed8b9da1-2f9e-5b3f-b37f-5208fd9750c2" :question/math-academy-id "q-49178" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/assets/ee37408e644416b0fe2d127703e6c5b531ae469e92d4119436fbb7f2b93ef573.png)\n\nA region in the $x$-$y$ plane is bounded by the curve $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{1}{x}$, the $x$-axis and the lines $x=1$ and $x=\\pi $, as shown above. The area of the region is" :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{\\pi }(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡x){|}_{1}^{\\pi } \\\\  & =(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi )-(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡1) \\\\  & =1+\\operatorname{ln}⁡\\pi +\\operatorname{cos}⁡1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304572 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ad216da-1bcf-5b87-9436-918ef1e5015a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Above a Curve and Below the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e201c8fd-1869-5ede-b6ad-0aed0618b063" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304574} {:answer/id #uuid "c20809de-5f82-506a-904c-5a4896f05924" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{32}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304575} {:answer/id #uuid "2e68784f-1248-5cb6-84f2-9859e21acd00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304576} {:answer/id #uuid "24eb3c35-0b2a-59b8-93bf-0aa48f818997" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304577} {:answer/id #uuid "69c92cc3-1574-57cc-8792-762701e9886e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304578}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c20809de-5f82-506a-904c-5a4896f05924" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{32}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304575} :answer-field/id #uuid "1c2c475a-8897-55ec-8804-225f2b7be9a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304573}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "882a6182-51b5-5a78-824c-d594efd5fdfc" :question/math-academy-id "q-54471" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/assets/d07ef9eb8b578cd9f5f0c2c57caa44760b0a5e21d95bb0961fcff722276a7b4e.png)\n\nFind the area between the curve $y={x}^{2}-4$, the $x$-axis and the line $x=-2$ and $x=2$, shown above." :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}({x}^{2}-4)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-4{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}|}_{-2}^{2}-4x{|}_{-2}^{2} \\\\  & =(\\frac{{2}^{3}}{3}-\\frac{(-2)^{3}}{3})-4(2+2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{32}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $\\frac{32}{3}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304579 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ad216da-1bcf-5b87-9436-918ef1e5015a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Area Bounded Above a Curve and Below the X-Axis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97c5c929-0700-57d5-8a9c-1ff7e0f766b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304581} {:answer/id #uuid "af2044c3-1653-5332-a43e-23eee49ddd9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304582} {:answer/id #uuid "f78485fc-7517-5100-9a14-f4418d4129b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304583} {:answer/id #uuid "3eccb8c1-1e76-5c28-a9f6-329a4e1d505a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304584} {:answer/id #uuid "ed73e557-deb4-572b-a8af-863efb48805b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304585}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f78485fc-7517-5100-9a14-f4418d4129b3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304583} :answer-field/id #uuid "2beaf8a0-e2ea-57ed-b579-5fecc375a1fe" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304580}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "690019f3-1842-5436-938c-1ec53c812f59" :question/math-academy-id "q-73324" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14039918/assets/333a99cd7b1f4aa0c3017c2b5aa42cb04acad842b19345a1176d57a71c5fd120.png)\n\nA region is bounded by the curve $y=-{sec}^{2}⁡x$, the $x$-axis and the lines $x=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and $x=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$, as shown above. Find the area of the region." :question/worked-solution "To find the area, we just need to compute the corresponding definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ={\\int }_{a}^{b}y(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4}(-{sec}^{2}⁡x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{tan}⁡x{|}_{-\\pi /4}^{\\pi /4} \\\\  & =-(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4})-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(-\\frac{\\pi }{4})) \\\\  & =-(1-(-1)) \\\\  & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we obtained a negative number. So the area that we want is $2.$"}]}
